format 1

# This repository's GitHub workflows (root T12, D26, paradigm/V28),
# rendered by `actlith gen` into .github/workflows/; never edit those by
# hand: the actlith-gen-check and actlith-check steps refuse drift.
#
# The gate kind runs the push gate, `hk check --all --check`, on every
# paradigm/V28 system GitHub hosts, with the pr0d1r2 cache, as lablith's
# row does. x86_64-darwin has no hosted runner in actlith 0.1.0 (it
# refuses the system), and the flake has no x86_64-darwin build of most
# fleet tools, so that system is gated by pre-push on the owner's Intel
# Mac, as paradigm/V28 has it: pre-push native on every owner laptop, CI
# the rest. The push gate builds the crate, runs every test, coverage and
# the release bench, so the job gets 60 minutes, not the default 30.
#
# There is no `build` row: it needs a flake package, and the flake has
# only the dev shell until `packages.default` lands (root T18).

## workflows
id|kind|systems|cache|args
ci|gate|x86_64-linux,aarch64-linux,aarch64-darwin|pr0d1r2|timeout=60
